# Independently authored KILL / BACKUP / RESTORE / PURGE
# sentinel smoke for the GPL MTR-format runner. NOT
# copied or adapted from MySQL's mysql-test/.
#
# Existing coverage (do NOT duplicate):
#   - KILL — NONE in compat-mtr (verified per PR #357
#     lesson).
#   - BACKUP DATABASE / RESTORE FROM — NONE.
#   - PURGE BINARY LOGS — NONE.
#   - mysql_maintenance_cmds_sentinel_basic_extra (PR
#     #371) covers FLUSH / RESET / HANDLER / SHUTDOWN.
#     This slice covers the remaining four ops/admin
#     statements that have NO zeta surface and
#     parse-reject at 1064.
#
# This slice pins:
#   - KILL <id> / KILL QUERY <id> / KILL CONNECTION <id>
#     → 1064 with the "unsupported statement: sqlparser::
#     ast::Statement" shape (parsed by sqlparser, rejected
#     in convert.rs:432-435).
#   - BACKUP DATABASE / RESTORE FROM / PURGE BINARY LOGS
#     → 1064 with the "Expected: an SQL statement, found:
#     <X>" shape (sqlparser doesn't recognize the leading
#     keyword).
#
# Big-picture finding (TWO-OF-FOUR ERROR-SHAPES):
#   These six statements span TWO of the four sqlparser
#   error templates documented in PR #371:
#
#   - **Shape (c)** "unsupported statement: sqlparser::
#     ast::Statement": KILL variants. Parsed by sqlparser
#     into a Statement::Kill variant; convert.rs:432-435
#     hits the catch-all reject.
#
#   - **Shape (d)** "Expected: an SQL statement, found:
#     <X>": BACKUP / RESTORE / PURGE. sqlparser-rs
#     doesn't recognize these as top-level statement
#     keywords at all — error fires at lexer/parser
#     level, before any AST is built.
#
#   No new shapes here — this slice is purely
#   completeness for the remaining sentinels not in PR
#   #371.
#
#   Recovery paths:
#
#   - KILL → use OS-level signaling (kill -INT or
#     supervisor restart). zeta has no per-connection
#     kill from SQL today.
#   - BACKUP DATABASE / RESTORE FROM → zeta uses
#     LSM-segment snapshots and log-replay for backup/
#     restore, not SQL-level commands. See the zeta
#     STORAGE_ENGINE_ANALYSIS.md for snapshot semantics.
#   - PURGE BINARY LOGS → zeta uses log-store
#     segments, not MySQL binlogs; rotation is internal
#     (no SQL handle).
#
# Adaptation notes:
#   # zeta-adapt: KILL <id> / KILL QUERY / KILL CONNECTION
#     all error 1064 (shape c). Use OS signaling for
#     connection lifecycle.
#   # zeta-adapt: BACKUP DATABASE / RESTORE FROM / PURGE
#     BINARY LOGS error 1064 (shape d). Backup/restore
#     are out-of-band ops in zeta; binlog purge is
#     internal.

--echo === KILL variants — shape (c) "unsupported statement" ===

--error 1064
KILL 123;
--error 1064
KILL QUERY 456;
--error 1064
KILL CONNECTION 789;

--echo === BACKUP / RESTORE / PURGE — shape (d) "Expected: an SQL statement" ===

--error 1064
BACKUP DATABASE test TO 'foo';
--error 1064
RESTORE FROM 'foo';
--error 1064
PURGE BINARY LOGS BEFORE '2026-01-01';
--error 1064
PURGE BINARY LOGS TO 'log';
